    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Jordyn Perez was about to turn eight years old when her mother suggested a new way to celebrate her birthday. “How about donating your gifts to a children’s hospital?” her mum asked."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Jordyn thought about the idea. She already had everything she needed. Children in hospital were facing real difficulties. They probably needed gifts more than she did. “Okay, that sounds cool,” she finally said."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Now Jordyn is in high school, but she has continued to bring joy to kids in hospital. Last Christmas, she made her tenth yearly gift donation to a children’s hospital in San Antonio, Texas."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Children can be in hospital for lots of reasons. In the United States, "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "asthma",
            "zh": "哮喘"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " is a top reason. But whatever the illness, a hospital stay can be "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "stressful",
            "ref": "v-stressful"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". Efforts like Jordyn’s are a bright spot during a difficult time."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Jordyn’s gift-giving project begins each year in November. When she sends her friends invitations to her birthday party, she includes a list of gift ideas for kids in hospital. Jordyn also shares the list with her family, her school volleyball coach, and teammates. The number of donations “grows every year”, she says. “We "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "measure",
            "ref": "v-measure"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " how much of the carpet they cover in our living room. Last year, they covered the "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "entire",
            "ref": "v-entire"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " carpet.” Then, it’s time to share the gifts with the children in the hospital. “Putting smiles on the faces of these little patients—that’s all I care about,” Jordyn says."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p6",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Jordyn has also encouraged others to follow in her footsteps. Some of her friends have collected and donated gifts for their birthdays. “It just makes you feel good to give to others,” Jordyn says. “I want to keep doing this as long as I can.”"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
